<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2025-08-11T06:46:37+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Mon, 11 Aug 2025 06:46:37 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title>‘Crime, murder, and death’: Trump slams Federal Reserve’s $3.1B renovation spending, vows to make capital ‘beautiful again’</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123225517.cms" /&gt;President Trump is set to address crime and beautification efforts in Washington, D.C., criticizing the Federal Reserve's renovation spending. He aims to eradicate crime, homelessness, and improve the capital's physical condition, establishing a task force for safety and beauty. Trump pledges to remove homeless individuals and incarcerate criminals, promising swift action and comparing it to border enforcement success.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/crime-murder-and-death-trump-slams-federal-reserves-3-1b-renovation-spending-vows-to-make-capital-beautiful-again/articleshow/123225517.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/crime-murder-and-death-trump-slams-federal-reserves-3-1b-renovation-spending-vows-to-make-capital-beautiful-again/articleshow/123225517.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T06:30:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123225834,imgsize-66598.cms"/></item><item><title>Israel-Gaza war: Five Al Jazeera journalists killed in Israeli strike; IDF claims one of correspondents served as 'terrorist cell leader in Hamas'</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123225024.cms" /&gt;An Israeli strike near Gaza City's Al-Shifa Hospital resulted in the deaths of at least five Al Jazeera journalists, including correspondent Mohammed Qreiqeh and camera operators. The IDF confirmed targeting Al Jazeera correspondent Anas al-Sharif, alleging he was a Hamas terrorist operative, a claim Al Jazeera denies.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-gaza-war-five-al-jazeera-journalists-killed-in-israeli-strike-idf-claims-one-of-correspondents-served-as-terrorist-cell-leader-in-hamas/articleshow/123225024.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-gaza-war-five-al-jazeera-journalists-killed-in-israeli-strike-idf-claims-one-of-correspondents-served-as-terrorist-cell-leader-in-hamas/articleshow/123225024.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T05:44:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123225275,imgsize-76992.cms"/></item><item><title>Chicago violence: 1 dead, 5 injured in mass shooting during outdoor gathering; additional attacks follow overnight</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123224059.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chicago-violence-1-dead-5-injured-in-mass-shooting-during-outdoor-gathering-additional-attacks-follow-overnight/articleshow/123224059.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chicago-violence-1-dead-5-injured-in-mass-shooting-during-outdoor-gathering-additional-attacks-follow-overnight/articleshow/123224059.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T04:04:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123224090,imgsize-1880977.cms"/></item><item><title>'Goal is to crush Putin's customers, India, China and Brazil': Lindsey Graham on Putin's 50% tariff</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123223446.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/goal-is-to-crush-putins-customers-india-china-and-brazil-lindsey-graham-on-putins-50-tariff/articleshow/123223446.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/goal-is-to-crush-putins-customers-india-china-and-brazil-lindsey-graham-on-putins-50-tariff/articleshow/123223446.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T01:45:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123223445,imgsize-31862.cms"/></item><item><title>'An abuse of system': Cuomo proposes 'Zohran's Law' to bar affluent New Yorkers from rent-stabilised apartments; suggests 'means test' in bill</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123223370.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/abuse-of-system-cuomo-proposes-zohrans-law-to-bar-affluent-new-yorkers-from-rent-stabilised-apartments-suggests-means-test-in-bill/articleshow/123223370.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/abuse-of-system-cuomo-proposes-zohrans-law-to-bar-affluent-new-yorkers-from-rent-stabilised-apartments-suggests-means-test-in-bill/articleshow/123223370.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T01:37:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123223421,imgsize-1036920.cms"/></item><item><title>UAE: Dubai now inviting AI experts and companies to collaborate on building AI-driven government services</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123219542.cms" /&gt;Dubai’s Centre for Artificial Intelligence has opened applications for the second cycle of its “Future of AI in Government Services Accelerator,” inviting global innovators to develop AI solutions with over 20 government entities. Running from October to November 2025, the program offers hands-on collaboration, sponsored accommodation, and access to senior decision-makers, aimed at transforming public services through AI innovation.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-dubai-now-inviting-ai-experts-and-companies-to-collaborate-on-building-ai-driven-government-services/articleshow/123219542.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-dubai-now-inviting-ai-experts-and-companies-to-collaborate-on-building-ai-driven-government-services/articleshow/123219542.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T01:20:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" u