msid-123222377,imgsize-614449.cms"/></item><item><title>Report: China detains diplomat for questioning after trip abroad</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123225637.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/report-china-detains-diplomat-for-questioning-after-trip-abroad/articleshow/123225637.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/report-china-detains-diplomat-for-questioning-after-trip-abroad/articleshow/123225637.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T06:12:16+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123225725,imgsize-583389.cms"/></item><item><title>Xi looks to tighten grip after scandals shake military elite</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123225758.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/xi-looks-to-tighten-grip-after-scandals-shake-military-elite/articleshow/123225758.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/xi-looks-to-tighten-grip-after-scandals-shake-military-elite/articleshow/123225758.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T06:20:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chris Buckley</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123225765,imgsize-8284.cms"/></item><item><title>Zelensky wins EU, Nato backing as he seeks place at Trump-Putin talks</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123225785.cms" /&gt;Volodymyr Zelensky seeks European and NATO support amidst concerns that a potential US-Russia summit could dictate terms unfavorable to Ukraine in the ongoing conflict. While Trump considers including Zelensky, Russia remains hesitant, raising fears of territorial concessions. European nations emphasize that any resolution must safeguard Ukraine's and Europe's security interests, with EU ministers convening to discuss further actions.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/zelensky-wins-eu-nato-backing-as-he-seeks-place-at-trump-putin-talks/articleshow/123225785.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/zelensky-wins-eu-nato-backing-as-he-seeks-place-at-trump-putin-talks/articleshow/123225785.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T06:22:42+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123225842,imgsize-1332440.cms"/></item><item><title>Deal unlikelyto satisfy either side: Vance</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123225599.cms" /&gt;US Vice President JD Vance anticipates that a negotiated resolution between Russia and Ukraine will likely displease both nations, as the US aims for a settlement acceptable to both. Vance mentioned the US is working to schedule discussions involving Putin, Zelensky, and Trump to explore a path toward ending the conflict, prioritizing a conversation between Putin and Trump beforehand.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/deal-unlikelyto-satisfy-either-side-vance/articleshow/123225599.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/deal-unlikelyto-satisfy-either-side-vance/articleshow/123225599.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-08-11T06:09:33+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123225613,imgsize-54762.cms"/></item><item><title>UN's Af female staff get threats, Taliban probe on</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123225574.cms" /&gt;</description